headings.text:
collapseTabset Collapse a tabset to just its header.
 This has no effect unless the tabset has the collapsible flag (or is floating; see FloatingTabsetNode);
the only tabset in a workspace, and tabsets whose siblings are all collapsed, can't be collapsed.

Number of columns a row gridline spans; defaults to all columns (starting from column).
 Gridlines can span a subset of columns in order to avoid cells that span across the boundary they sit on;
multiple gridlines can be rendered along the same boundary (e.g. before and after a spanning cell).

Number of rows a column gridline spans; defaults to all rows (starting from row).
 Gridlines can span a subset of rows in order to avoid cells that span across the boundary they sit on;
multiple gridlines can be rendered along the same boundary (e.g. above and below a spanning cell).
